<title>USA: Stonegate District, Colo., yields 5.70 pct in 2025.</title>
<headline>Stonegate District, Colo., yields 5.70 pct in 2025.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hanifen Imhoff Inc said Tuesday it tentatively priced $42.1 million bonds and $3.1 million taxable notes for Stonegate Village Metropolitan District, Colo., at a top tax-exempt yield of 5.70 percent in 2025.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>STONEGATE VILLAGE METROPOLITAN DISTRICT</p>
<p>DOUGLAS COUNTY, COLO.</p>
<p>$42,055,000 GENERAL OBLIGATION REFUNDING AND IMPROVEMENT BONDS</p>
<p>SERIES 1996A</p>
<p>$3,100,000</p>
<p>GENERAL OBLIGATION TAXABLE REFUNDING AND IMPROVEMENT BONDS</p>
<p>SERIES 1996B</p>
<p>DATED: 11/1/1996</p>
<p>RATINGS: MOODY'S Aaa, S&amp;P AAA</p>
<p>FSA INSURED</p>
<p>FIRST COUPON 6/1/1997</p>
<p>DELIVERY EST: 11/27/1996</p>
<p>CALLABLE: 12/1/2006 @ 101.00</p>
<p>	    12/1/2008 @ 100.00</p>
<p>BOOK ENTRY ONLY</p>
<p>BONDS MATURING 12/1/2011 SUBJECT TO EXTRAORDINARY REDEMPTION</p>
<p>$42.055 million GO refunding and improvement bonds</p>
